# Rust-repo-first development

All new development — new crates, new features, bug fixes, tests, and CI
changes — happens in the Rust workspace at the root of this repo
(`crates/*`), not in the reference submodules.

The directories under `submodules/` (`coda-agents`, `coda-app`,
`Coda-Computer-Use`, `coda-gym`) are **reference material**. Do not:

- ❌ Edit any file under `submodules/**`
- ❌ Add crates, tests, or scripts inside a submodule
- ❌ Create PR branches against a submodule repository

Instead:

- ✅ Put new Rust code in a crate under `crates/`
- ✅ Put new tests alongside the crate they exercise (`crates/<name>/tests/`)
- ✅ Reuse submodule code by reading it for reference, then implementing the
  needed logic in the workspace crate that owns the concern
- ✅ If a change genuinely belongs in a product repository, stop and raise it
  with the user before touching anything

## ❌ BAD

```text
submodules/coda-app/backend/app/services/new_feature.py   # editing a submodule
submodules/coda-agents/src/adapters/.../new_module.rs     # editing a submodule
```

## ✅ GOOD

```text
crates/duet-api/src/new_feature.rs        # workspace crate
crates/duet-api/tests/new_feature.rs      # tests next to the crate
```

Check before writing: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` should print the
coda-rust root, and the file path must not start with `submodules/`.
